00:32:03.088 --> 00:32:05.966
He said that we had this look in our eyes then.

00:32:07.384 --> 00:32:10.137
That we didn't flinch or turn away.

00:32:13.265 --> 00:32:16.101
That's when he decided to raise us as yakuzas.

00:32:16.893 --> 00:32:18.645
That look in our eyes.

00:32:22.190 --> 00:32:24.901
When I saw your niece, I saw the same look in hers.

00:32:25.652 --> 00:32:26.820
You have it too.

00:32:28.530 --> 00:32:29.990
And I know I still have it.

00:32:31.116 --> 00:32:32.909
That's just the type of people we are.

00:32:33.702 --> 00:32:37.788
If you keep a lion locked in a cage, her claws will get dull.

00:32:37.789 --> 00:32:39.583
She'll forget her own nature.

00:32:44.504 --> 00:32:46.464
I guess the choice is yours now.

00:32:47.215 --> 00:32:50.385
Not true. It's Jian's to make.

00:32:51.553 --> 00:32:53.471
Considering the bad choices I made,

00:32:54.556 --> 00:32:56.849
I don't think it's a luxury I deserve.

00:32:56.850 --> 00:32:59.393
Jian has already made her choice,

00:32:59.394 --> 00:33:02.564
So what I'll do now is protect her with everything in me.

00:33:10.322 --> 00:33:11.656
I think this is

00:33:14.201 --> 00:33:15.577
As far as I can go.

00:33:24.044 --> 00:33:27.547
Do you think we can meet again one day?

00:33:30.550 --> 00:33:31.843
If we're still breathing.

00:33:33.428 --> 00:33:36.014
Looks like that drink will have to wait again.

00:33:40.227 --> 00:33:41.436
My name is

00:33:43.480 --> 00:33:44.564
Ichika, okay?

00:33:47.108 --> 00:33:49.778
Takimoto Ichika.

00:34:09.464 --> 00:34:10.798
Report this to Q right away.

00:34:10.799 --> 00:34:11.800
Shit, we're fucked.

00:34:15.887 --> 00:34:19.181
Q, come in. Answer me now!

00:34:19.182 --> 00:34:21.101
:cue

00:34:28.024 --> 00:34:30.901
- What? I'm busy here. -  We have a serious problem.

00:34:30.902 --> 00:34:32.152
The higher-ups know everything.

00:34:32.153 --> 00:34:34.446
You need to come to the office immediately.

00:34:34.447 --> 00:34:37.117
I was told "a certain person" is waiting for you on a video call.

00:34:41.913 --> 00:34:42.914
Shit.

00:34:44.416 --> 00:34:46.126
Has headquarters said anything?

00:34:50.714 --> 00:34:52.716
Shit. No.

00:35:17.324 --> 00:35:19.534
Oh, shit. Son of a bitch.

00:35:20.952 --> 00:35:21.953
Don't move!

00:35:24.748 --> 00:35:25.749
It's all right.

00:35:31.379 --> 00:35:35.008
Hey, lower the guns. Yeah, it's all right. It's dangerous.

00:35:54.819 --> 00:35:55.986
-  Yes? -  K,

00:35:55.987 --> 00:35:57.447
Pull out of there immediately

00:35:57.739 --> 00:35:59.574
- and return to headquarters. -  Sorry?

00:36:00.784 --> 00:36:01.868
Do you mean right now?

00:36:03.411 --> 00:36:05.287
We're in the middle of an operation.

00:36:05.288 --> 00:36:08.666
From now on, that operation has nothing to do with Babylon.

00:36:08.667 --> 00:36:10.543
Return to base. Immediately.

00:36:15.256 --> 00:36:16.466
Huh?

00:36:17.634 --> 00:36:20.053
It's not like I'm busy as hell or anything.

00:36:21.054 --> 00:36:22.764
If it's urgent, he should come himself.

00:36:57.090 --> 00:36:58.091
Where to?

00:37:06.391 --> 00:37:07.892
Let's go home.

00:37:37.630 --> 00:37:39.924
:cue

00:37:57.233 --> 00:37:58.984
Hey, did you see the bus footage?

00:37:58.985 --> 00:38:00.612
Yeah, what a crazy bitch.

00:38:06.993 --> 00:38:09.204
I knew something was off from the start. Shit.

00:38:53.039 --> 00:38:56.835
Are you fucking kidding me?

00:39:34.080 --> 00:39:35.123
DISABLE SECURITY PROTOCOL?

00:39:50.221 --> 00:39:51.389
Stay out here.

00:40:33.681 --> 00:40:36.601
You sneaky motherfucker.

00:40:58.039 --> 00:41:01.625
Hey, main gate. Stop that vehicle from entering!

00:41:01.626 --> 00:41:02.918
Stop that goddamn bus!

00:41:02.919 --> 00:41:04.294
That the reason the bus exploded

00:41:04.295 --> 00:41:05.712
- that night was -  Can't you hear me?

00:41:05.713 --> 00:41:07.757
- to cover up Bale killing Jun. -  Do you wanna die too?

00:41:09.300 --> 00:41:11.803
:cue

00:41:17.433 --> 00:41:18.434
Okay.

00:41:21.729 --> 00:41:24.816
Seems like Operation Empty House is a success.

00:41:25.942 --> 00:41:29.862
All we're doing is using her own playbook and turning it back on her.

00:41:57.932 --> 00:42:00.685
How the hell did that bastard get out of that damn cell?

00:42:27.670 --> 00:42:28.671
What should we do?

00:42:53.821 --> 00:42:56.908
Let's just wait. Just a bit.

00:43:06.584 --> 00:43:09.003
Lower your guns. Everyone, guns down.

00:43:11.672 --> 00:43:12.673
Open the gate.

00:43:18.262 --> 00:43:20.180
You all heard, I'm sure,

00:43:20.181 --> 00:43:23.684
Most of Babylon's fighters have been buried under tons of rubble in our mine.

00:43:24.435 --> 00:43:27.229
We expect that some number of forces will remain,

00:43:27.230 --> 00:43:29.190
But our target is only

00:43:30.441 --> 00:43:31.776
Kusanagi Jin.

00:43:32.693 --> 00:43:34.444
If they aren't targets,

00:43:34.445 --> 00:43:38.324
Please refrain from engaging with any unarmed personnel that are still inside.

00:43:39.784 --> 00:43:41.202
Just priority one.

00:43:46.082 --> 00:43:50.043
So these trashy little vermin really want to come after me, huh?

00:43:50.044 --> 00:43:53.840
These fucking rat bastards. I have to do everything around here.

00:43:57.802 --> 00:44:01.264
In the end, you're all you got. Fucking alone.

00:44:10.314 --> 00:44:11.315
Shit.

00:44:24.078 --> 00:44:25.872
:cue

00:44:36.382 --> 00:44:37.383
Three o'clock.

00:45:14.503 --> 00:45:16.547
You dressed correctly for the occasion.

00:45:34.649 --> 00:45:35.650
Let's do this.

00:45:36.525 --> 00:45:38.277
The real negotiation begins now.

00:45:42.198 --> 00:45:43.199
Hey!

00:45:46.202 --> 00:45:48.996
Come and get me, you ragtag motherfuckers!

00:46:00.007 --> 00:46:01.466
Uncle

00:46:01.467 --> 00:46:02.593
Are you okay?

00:46:09.058 --> 00:46:11.894
Hey! Kusanagi's in front of the situation room!

00:46:34.166 --> 00:46:35.334
Jian, get up!

00:46:43.843 --> 00:46:44.927
Hold as long as you can.

00:47:01.235 --> 00:47:02.653
Not a fucking chance.

00:47:18.336 --> 00:47:19.337
We're connected.

00:47:35.436 --> 00:47:38.272
So you are Jeong Jinman.

00:47:45.321 --> 00:47:48.824
It's been 12 years since I've had to smell this disgusting gunpowder!

00:48:01.045 --> 00:48:05.257
Are you trying to blackmail us with something Kusanagi did on her own?

00:48:07.051 --> 00:48:08.552
That seems a little weak.

00:48:09.095 --> 00:48:11.806
I'm just relaying to you what your employee did

00:48:12.723 --> 00:48:14.892
During her time here leading Babylon Korea.

00:48:15.976 --> 00:48:19.105
The blackmail would be the data we have on the server.

00:48:30.449 --> 00:48:32.243
What is it that you want?

00:48:32.868 --> 00:48:35.663
Peaceful coexistence between murthehelp and Babylon.

00:48:36.497 --> 00:48:37.706
That's all I want.

00:48:44.046 --> 00:48:45.714
"Peaceful coexistence."

00:48:48.217 --> 00:48:51.262
Do you think such an idealistic relationship can last?

00:48:52.596 --> 00:48:57.059
Peace isn't exactly good for our line of business.

00:48:59.770 --> 00:49:03.064
I'm sure you know this since you were once a part of Babylon,

00:49:03.065 --> 00:49:05.859
But we will not hesitate to break any lasting peace

00:49:05.860 --> 00:49:07.653
For the sake of business.

00:49:08.362 --> 00:49:13.409
Humans have been killing each other for thousands of years now,

00:49:14.452 --> 00:49:18.831
And in the end your murthehelp is banking on that same human nature,

00:49:19.498 --> 00:49:21.500
Making profit off human lives. :cue

00:49:22.626 --> 00:49:25.880
For someone like that to be talking about peace

00:49:28.591 --> 00:49:29.967
What a contradiction.

00:49:34.054 --> 00:49:37.391
There have been times of peace, no matter how brief they were.

00:49:38.434 --> 00:49:39.560
In that case

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:43.355
We can call it a ceasefire.

00:49:48.277 --> 00:49:51.489
If Babylon were to accept my proposal,

00:49:52.448 --> 00:49:54.909
I won't need murthehelp. Not anymore.

00:50:07.963 --> 00:50:10.591
-  Uncle Cheolseung! - Don't worry, I'm okay.

00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:19.683
Who the hell said you could negotiate by yourselves?

00:50:22.520 --> 00:50:23.812
Put the gun down.

00:50:24.939 --> 00:50:26.649
Your work here is finished now.

00:50:29.109 --> 00:50:33.696
My methods were never a problem before. You'd just turn a blind eye, didn't you?

00:50:33.697 --> 00:50:37.535
I did it all for the sake of Babylon. And now what? You're firing me?

00:50:38.577 --> 00:50:41.496
All because of a lapse of judgment?

00:50:41.497 --> 00:50:45.417
It was never "all for the sake of Babylon" to you.

00:50:46.168 --> 00:50:48.170
You were only ever loyal to yourself.

00:50:52.049 --> 00:50:53.133
Fuck that!

00:50:55.678 --> 00:50:57.345
You pathetic little shits.

00:51:37.136 --> 00:51:38.137
Mr. Jeong Jinman

00:51:40.556 --> 00:51:45.019
You and I are both people who walk alongside the specter of death.

00:51:47.187 --> 00:51:50.482
I swear, as long as I remain here

00:51:52.943 --> 00:51:54.653
I'll honor our ceasefire.

00:51:55.446 --> 00:51:56.614
We have a truce.

00:51:58.616 --> 00:52:01.952
Then I'll take care of business over here.

00:52:03.245 --> 00:52:04.246
But first

00:52:05.998 --> 00:52:07.707
I'll make this clear.

00:52:07.708 --> 00:52:10.835
Even if the most trivial piece of data leaks out,

00:52:10.836 --> 00:52:13.964
For example, let's say, what a client had for dinner

00:52:14.673 --> 00:52:16.883
Or the name of our client's dog.

00:52:16.884 --> 00:52:18.886
If anything were to leak out,

00:52:19.637 --> 00:52:21.013
Then you and your niece,

00:52:21.764 --> 00:52:25.684
Along with anyone ever involved with your operation,

00:52:27.353 --> 00:52:28.479
Will all disappear.

00:52:32.983 --> 00:52:35.027
Make sure you honor your end.

00:52:40.908 --> 00:52:43.869
We'll talk again, Jeong Jinman.

00:52:45.162 --> 00:52:46.205
And you too

00:52:48.290 --> 00:52:49.416
Jeong Jian.

00:53:36.380 --> 00:53:37.840
Did everyone make it out?

00:54:29.224 --> 00:54:30.350
Now what's the plan?

00:54:33.103 --> 00:54:34.396
You're asking me that?

00:54:48.702 --> 00:54:49.703
Then now

00:54:54.249 --> 00:54:56.834
Listen up, Jeong Jinman.

00:54:56.835 --> 00:55:01.632
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

00:55:09.681 --> 00:55:11.141
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG

